{"id":"b40331e7-0401-43ec-90b2-c3e0ba52afc3","object":"chat.completion","created":1785015152,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('case must be a dict')\\n    word_token_indices = case.get('word_token_indices')\\n    word_scores = case.get('word_scores')\\n    forced_words = case.get('forced_words', [])\\n    token_budget = case.get('token_budget')\\n    if not all([word_token_indices, word_scores, token_budget is not None]):\\n        raise ValueError('Missing required fields')\\n    n = len(word_token_indices)\\n    if len(word_scores) != n:\\n        raise ValueError('Mismatched lengths')\\n    # validate indices in forced_words are within range and no duplicates\\n    if not all(0 <= i < n for i in forced_words):\\n        raise ValueError('Invalid forced word index')\\n    # token counts per word\\n    token_counts = [len(indices) for indices in word_token_indices]\\n    # sum forced tokens\\n    forced_tokens = sum(token_counts[i] for i in forced_words)\\n    if forced_tokens > token_budget:\\n        raise ValueError('Forced words exceed token budget')\\n    # list of candidate words (not forced)\\n    candidates = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        if i not in forced_words:\\n            candidates.append((i, word_scores[i], token_counts[i]))\\n    # sort by descending score, then ascending index\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (-x[1], x[0]))\\n    selected = set(forced_words)\\n    remaining_budget = token_budget - forced_tokens\\n    for idx, score, tcnt in candidates:\\n        if tcnt <= remaining_budget:\\n            selected.add(idx)\\n            remaining_budget -= tcnt\\n    # build output in original order\\n    selected_words = sorted(selected)  # original order\\n    retained_token_indices = []\\n    for i in selected_words:\\n        retained_token_indices.extend(word_token_indices[i])\\n    tokens_used = sum(token_counts[i] for i in selected_words)\\n    return {\\n        'retained_token_indices': retained_token_indices,\\n        'selected_words': selected_words,\\n        'tokens_used': tokens_used\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python solve(case) that implements the described algorithm. The task: Given word_token_indices (list of lists of token indices, each sublist corresponds to a word), word_scores (list of floats), forced_words (list of indices of words that must be selected), token_budget (integer). Must select words (each word either fully selected or not) such that forced_words are included, and total tokens used <= token_budget. If forced_words already exceed budget, raise ValueError. Otherwise, greedily select additional words based on descending score (and then by original index for ties) until budget exhausted. Return: retained_token_indices (list of token indices of selected words, in original order), selected_words (list of indices of selected words, in original order), tokens_used (total number of tokens). Must not mutate input. Use only Python standard library.\n\nImplementation details: parse case dict, extract fields. Validate types, existence, etc. Compute total tokens of forced words. If > budget, raise ValueError. Then create list of candidate words (indices not forced) with their scores and token counts. Sort by descending score, then ascending index (since we want original order for ties? Actually ties: \"Rank remaining words by descending supplied score and then source position.\" Source position = i in list. So sort by (-score, i). Then iterate, for each candidate if adding its tokens does not exceed remaining budget, add it. Then after selection, build results: selected_words (list of word indices in original order, includes forced). retained_token_indices: concatenate token indices from selected words in original order. tokens_used: sum of lengths. Return dict.\n\nNeed to handle edge cases: forced_words list may be empty. Ensure we don't include duplicate forced words? Assume forced_words given as distinct. If forced word index out of range, raise ValueError.\n\nOutput schema requires keys: retained_token_indices, selected_words, tokens_used.\n\nWe'll write solve(case) that returns a dict.\n\nFinally, wrap implementation as a JSON string under key \"implementation\". No markdown, just JSON.\n\nLet's craft the Python code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1472,"completion_tokens":967,"total_tokens":2439,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":442},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":64},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}